    <comp lib="0" loc="(20,27)" name="Text">
      <a name="halign" val="left"/>
      <a name="text">a clumsy 120 hz triangle wave generator - When enabled, it counts up to 10000, then counts
down to -10000, then back up again to 10000, etc., forever.  It counts by 400 at a time, so
at 16kHz simulation speed, this produces a 120 Hz triangle wave (since it goes through 50 steps
on the way up, and 50 steps on the way down, for 100 steps per wave, and 16000/100 = 160).</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(234,519)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="57"/>
      <a name="dy" val="34"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#cc45bf"/>
      <a name="halign" val="right"/>
      <a name="text">This part keeps track of 
which direction we want 
to count (0=up, 1=down).
</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(502,123)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="-144"/>
      <a name="dy" val="57"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#cc45bf"/>
      <a name="text">These two comparisons are checking 
to see if the counter equals +25 (hit bottom)
or if it equals -25 (hit top)</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(505,630)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="-106"/>
      <a name="dy" val="-33"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#cc45bf"/>
      <a name="text">This part makes it change 
direction when we 
"hit top" OR "hit bottom".
But if en=0, it goes
back to "up" direction.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(542,409)" name="Callout">
      <a name="background" val="#feffa189"/>
      <a name="dx" val="-74"/>
      <a name="dy" val="-56"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#cc45bf"/>
      <a name="text">16 bit signed audio samples in range [-10000, +10000]
meant to be played using 16 kHz audio PCM output.
This is the result of taking the counter, which is
in the range [-25, +25], and multiplying it by 400.</a>
    </comp>
