  <circuit name="sweep-0-to-65535">
    <a name="appearance" val="custom"/>
    <appear>
      <rect fill="none" height="60" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="2" width="80" x="50" y="50"/>
      <text dominant-baseline="central" font-family="SansSerif" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" x="102" y="57">sweep 0</text>
      <polyline fill="none" points="79,76 79,96" stroke="#000000"/>
      <polyline fill="none" points="99,76 99,96" stroke="#000000"/>
      <polyline fill="none" points="59,96 79,76" stroke="#000000"/>
      <polyline fill="none" points="79,96 99,76" stroke="#000000"/>
      <polyline fill="none" points="99,96 119,76" stroke="#000000"/>
      <visible-probe height="10" path="/Probe(100,450)" stroke-width="0" width="53" x="44" y="99"/>
      <polyline fill="none" points="56,96 119,96" stroke="#b8b8b8"/>
      <visible-rgbled height="10" path="/RGBLED(150,340)" stroke-width="0" width="10" x="53" y="51"/>
      <text dominant-baseline="central" font-family="SansSerif" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" x="103" y="69">to 65535</text>
      <circ-port height="8" pin="140,310" width="8" x="46" y="56"/>
      <circ-port height="10" pin="420,300" width="10" x="125" y="85"/>
      <circ-port height="8" pin="90,500" width="8" x="66" y="106"/>
      <circ-port height="8" pin="140,370" width="8" x="46" y="66"/>
      <circ-anchor facing="east" height="6" width="6" x="127" y="87"/>
    </appear>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(125,138)" name="Callout">
      <a name="background" val="#feffa189"/>
      <a name="dx" val="39"/>
      <a name="dy" val="65"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#cc45bf"/>
      <a name="text">The heart of this circuit is a
 32-bit value, with a feedback loop
adding "step" during each clock tick.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(18,39)" name="Text">
      <a name="halign" val="left"/>
      <a name="text">a flexible but LOUD and UNSIGNED sawtooth generator - When enabled, counts from 0
up to 65535, then resets to 0, and counts up again, forever. It counts upwards at a speed
determined by one of the inputs, you can choose any frequency from 1Hz to 4095Hz.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(297,448)" name="Text">
      <a name="halign" val="left"/>
      <a name="text">The counter up above is 32-bits, going from about -2billion to 2 billion,
before wrapping around to -2billion again. Each simulated clock tick we
add some "step" to the counter, so if the simulation is running
at 16kHz for audio output, we'd wrap around this often:
     F=(16000*stepsize)/4billion  wraparounds per second.
In other words, that's the frequency of the sawtooth we
generated.  Inversely, if we want a given frequency F,
we can calculate the needed stepsize to get it:
  stepsize = F*4billion/16000
                 = F*268435.46
</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(40,636)" name="Text">
      <a name="foreground" val="#002bed"/>
      <a name="halign" val="left"/>
      <a name="text">Q: Why is this using a 32-bit counter instead of 16 bits?
A: Because it lets us adjust the step size more finely,
more precisly controlling exactly how long it takes to
reach the maximum and wrap around back to zero.

With a 32-bit counter (0 to 4billion), we have a lot
of possible step sizes to choose from to control how
often the counter wraps around.
</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(419,357)" name="Callout">
      <a name="background" val="#feffa189"/>
      <a name="dx" val="-27"/>
      <a name="dy" val="-37"/>
      <a name="foreground" val="#cc45bf"/>
      <a name="text">This "requantizer" divides by 2^16, so
the large counter values are scaled down
but exactly fill the output range [0, 65535]</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="0" loc="(466,133)" name="Text">
      <a name="foreground" val="#8a3bd4"/>
      <a name="halign" val="left"/>
      <a name="text">Q: Why is the frequency limited a 4095hz? Can we go higher?
A: The "Freq" input is a 12 bit number, which maxes out at 4095.
It would be simple to allow higher numbers, by using more bits
for "Freq". But with 16kHz PCM audio, we are limited to 8000hz
maximum anyway, and sounds above 4000hz sound pretty high
anyway.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="1" loc="(100,450)" name="Probe">
      <a name="facing" val="south"/>
      <a name="radix" val="10unsigned"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="1" loc="(140,240)" name="Tunnel">
      <a name="facing" val="east"/>
      <a name="label" val="step"/>
      <a name="width" val="32"/>
    </comp>
